      "writtenOn": "2025-01-07T22:08:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe we can have a `Set` function as well on this which sets the data and returns `true` iff we overrode something? Then in the the `Set*` functions we could just call with the offset from `*ByteLayouts`?\n\ni.e.\n\n```\ntemplate \u003ctypename In\u003e\nbool Set(uint32_t offset, In in) {\n    DAWN_ASSERT(sizeof(In) + offset \u003c\u003d sizeof(T));\n    if (memcmp(Get\u003cIn\u003e(offset), \u0026in), sizeof(In)) !\u003d 0) {\n        *reinterpret_cast\u003cIn*\u003e(\u0026mData[offset]) \u003d in;\n        return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n}\n```\n\nThen in something like `SetNumWorkgroups`, we could have:\n\n```\nSetNumWorkgroups(uint32_t numWorkgroupX,\n                 uint32_t numWorkgroupY,\n                 uint32_t numWorkgroupZ) {\n    bool constantBlockDirty \u003d false;\n\n    constantBlockDirty |\u003d\n        mContent.Set(\n            ComputeImmediateConstantsBytesLayout::NumWorkgroupsX,\n            numWorkgroupX\n        );\n    constantBlockDirty |\u003d\n        mContent.Set(\n            ComputeImmediateConstantsBytesLayout::NumWorkgroupsY,\n            numWorkgroupY\n        );\n    constantBlockDirty |\u003d\n        mContent.Set(\n            ComputeImmediateConstantsBytesLayout::NumWorkgroupsZ,\n            numWorkgroupZ\n        );\n    ...\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 5
      },
